# Allowlist: exclude everything, then re-admit only what the build reads.
#
# A denylist silently ships whatever nobody remembered to add — that is how a
# 45MB agent cache and the full 30MB git history ended up in the build context.
# With this form, a new dotfile, cache directory or credential file is excluded
# by default and has to be opted in deliberately.
*

# Go module graph
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Sources (the embedded AWS data lives under internal/spot/data)
!cmd/
!internal/

# Build driver
!Makefile

# Re-exclude things that would otherwise ride in under the directories above.
# Tests and mocks are not build inputs; the binary is built from non-test files.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
**/.DS_Store

# Never ship credentials or local env, even if a pattern above would admit them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.aws/
**/.ssh/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials

# Caches and scratch output
**/*.bak
**/*.tmp
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html
